g" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/00/374400/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5a23ab9ef5354927bac8c9663140a1431992adce" commit="a4c76ab89db9a97d295b69bc4d93d5c4b4ec4234" commit_message="factory_netboot: Change build target name to factory_netboot.  The chromeos-initramfs now builds factory netboot folder with name 'factory_netboot' so we should stop overriding the target name.  BUG=chromium:477744 TEST=make; build_packages; build_image; make_netboot.sh CQ-DEPEND=CL:374200,CL:374400  Change-Id: I5a23ab9ef5354927bac8c9663140a1431992adce Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/374878 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="6" gerrit_number="374878" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/initramfs" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/initramfs" ref="refs/changes/78/374878/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="6"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e14a69c56af4457d6bc61bf2bf334cd594cc131" commit="0286e19fae808ddd53445544060dc3f6632c2b5a" commit_message="chromeos-initramfs: Change 'netboot_ramfs' to right name 'factory_netboot_ramfs'.  The 'netboot_ramfs' was actually referring to 'factory netboot' in initramfs folder and should be renamed to be consistent.  The build rules are also simplified due to the new consistent names.  BUG=chromium:477744 TEST=build_packages; build_image factory_install;      build_image; mod_image_for_recovery.sh;      make_netboot.sh CQ-DEPEND=CL:374878,CL:374400  Change-Id: I5e14a69c56af4457d6bc61bf2bf334cd594cc131 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/374200 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="374200" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/00/374200/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibe857665be46965c52d4b4ff6f0f84dd63574373" commit="84efdfbd3da7bdbba16fc3d4cf6f728d3e81a785" commit_message="CRAS: iodev - Add state variable in cras_iodev  Reland e9e2c8e CRAS: iodev - Add state variable in cras_iodev.  The bug in cras_iodev_open for input device has been fixed. Since input device start in the end of open, its state should be normal run. Also fix the unittest that failed to catch this issue.  Use state variable to maintain the state of iodev. Remove no_stream_state flag in iodev. Remove is_open ops in iodev. Remove dev_running ops in iodev.  Now iodev uses start ops to determine if a device can stay in open state. If start ops is not supported, device should start running right after opening. Output device will be in no_stream state, while input device will be in normal state.  This is in preparation for the next patch to move state transition from write_output_samples in audio_thread into cras_iodev and cleanup iodev interface.  BUG=chromium:519942 TEST=make check  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364432 Change-Id: Ibe857665be46965c52d4b4ff6f0f84dd63574373 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375581 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375581" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/81/375581/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I942b52cc6fb14dc74df8cf808999244738603c80" commit="a22ae7c0ebd20f3bb488d36cd80523f6008cc1c3" commit_message="CRAS: iodev - Move no stream state transition into cras_iodev  Reland 2a98fae CRAS: iodev - Move no stream state transition into cras_iodev.  Previously, cras_iodev state transition is done in audio_thread write_output_samples function. Now state transition is triggered by sample ready event and stream removal event, where these events are detected in cras_iodev_output_possibly_transit_state and cras_iodev_rm_stream.  cras_iodev_start is removed from public API since it will be called within cras_iodev during state transition.  write_output_samples is simplified such that it can check the state after possible transition and write samples from stream if device is in normal state.  BUG=chromium:519942 TEST=unittest  Change-Id: I942b52cc6fb14dc74df8cf808999244738603c80 Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364433 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375845 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375845" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/45/375845/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2aeee9a56f487b368d46ec318df2b4c0c6e73082" commit="0e2dc801ebaec9f2140fc6d9545df5f6a3948e32" commit_message="media-sound/adhd: Adding systemd unit files  BUG=chromium:583671 CQ-DEPEND=CL:373379 TEST=Built packages.  Change-Id: I2aeee9a56f487b368d46ec318df2b4c0c6e73082 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/